# The scenes of the junit-extensions deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# junit-extensions.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in junit-extensions.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the shop's settings
note "A line on a shop receipt reads the *shop-wide settings*: prices with VAT or not, and the rate."
show ShopReceipt 4 11 "a shop receipt line" --zoom 7-8

## Scene 2: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's trade invoice. It switches a shop-wide setting off, and leaves it off."
show TodaysTradeInvoice 8 15 "today's trade invoice" --zoom 12

## Scene 3: set-up by hand
note "Tests with *set-up by hand*: the settings set once, before all the tests, and never put back."
show HandSetUpTest 12 32 "tests set up by hand" --zoom 15-19

## Scene 4: the extension
note "A *JUnit extension*: standard settings before each test, put back after, and a check nothing leaked."
show StandardShopSettings 11 31 "the extension" --zoom 19-21,26-29 --mark 11

## Scene 5: tests that use it
note "The same tests, with *no set-up* of their own: one line asks JUnit to use the extension."
show GuardedSettingsTest 11 27 "tests that use the extension" --zoom 12

## Scene 6: the leak is caught
note "Run both sets of tests against today's trade invoice:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:junit-extensions:test -Pcode=today"
callout "By hand, the innocent receipt test fails. The extension fails the test that left the setting changed."

## Scene 7: the fixed trade invoice
note "The trade invoice that writes its own price without VAT, and leaves the settings alone:"
show FixedTradeInvoice 7 13 "the fixed trade invoice" --zoom 11
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:junit-extensions:test"
callout "Every test passes. The extension sets up and cleans up for every test that uses it."
